---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Accessibility statement" crumbLabel="Accessibility statement">
  <div class="page-head">
    <h1>Accessibility statement</h1>
    <p class="lede">calenda11y is built to meet WCAG 2.2 at level AAA, the highest level.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="flow">
    <h2>What you can do on this site</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Use it with a keyboard, a screen reader, voice control or switch access.</li>
      <li>Zoom up to 400% without the page breaking or scrolling sideways.</li>
      <li>
        Change the colours, text size and spacing in <a href="/settings">display settings</a>.
      </li>
      <li>Use every feature without JavaScript.</li>
      <li>Take as long as you need. Nothing on this site times out.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>How we test</h2>
    <p>
      Every page is checked automatically on every change, for colour contrast, keyboard access, focus visibility, valid
      code and the automated WCAG checks in axe. People also test it with screen readers before each release.
    </p>
    <h2>Known limits</h2>
    <p>
      Event names, summaries and descriptions are written by organisers, sometimes in other languages. We ask for a
      plain-language summary of every event, but we can't guarantee the reading level of text we didn't write.
    </p>
    <h2>Tell us about a problem</h2>
    <p>
      If something on calenda11y doesn't work for you, email
      <a href="mailto:accessibility@calenda11y.org">accessibility@calenda11y.org</a>. We aim to reply within 5 working
      days.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
